WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.850 --> 00:00:03.462
Open the battery-charger sample: a complete drawing set, 25 pages.

2
00:00:03.712 --> 00:00:08.038
The cover sheet: every sheet with its revision, issue status and the customer's approval.

3
00:00:08.288 --> 00:00:14.296
Contents, single-line, and the PLC page with its I/O card.

4
00:00:14.546 --> 00:00:21.323
Place a contactor coil from the library: its designation is assigned by itself.

5
00:00:21.573 --> 00:00:32.895
Place its contact: same device, and the cross-references appear on both.

6
00:00:33.145 --> 00:00:36.307
Give the device a part from the library: the BOM will know about it.

7
00:00:36.557 --> 00:00:41.275
Number the wires with your own pattern: 020L+, 021L+ ...

8
00:00:41.525 --> 00:00:44.416
The wire list follows the schematic ...

9
00:00:44.666 --> 00:00:48.121
... and the BOM already counts the new contactor.

10
00:00:48.371 --> 00:00:54.270
Draw a wire that connects to nothing: the check banner finds it at once.

11
00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:57.115
One click on the fix, and the problem is gone.

12
00:00:57.365 --> 00:01:00.230
PLC I/O: every channel with address, tag and what it is wired to.

13
00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:09.180
Edit a tag here, export the tag list for the PLC tool.

14
00:01:09.430 --> 00:01:11.820
Export the PDF drawing set ...

15
00:01:12.070 --> 00:01:14.784
... and every list as one XLSX workbook.

16
00:01:15.034 --> 00:01:25.943
Sizing: the motor is raised to 7.5 kW and the feeder is sized from the schematic.

17
00:01:26.193 --> 00:01:30.006
The contactor that meets the requirement and is in stock, with warehouse and location: select and confirm.

18
00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:35.254
The BOM shows the new part with on hand, available and location.

19
00:01:35.504 --> 00:01:38.795
CablePilot: free, open source, your files stay yours.
